## 🔴 P0 — Critical (Release Blockers, Runtime Hangs & Compiler Errors)

### [ ] T01: Fix `autoVars()` Options Object Parameter Causing 1ms Infinite Loop
- **Files:** [`src/adapters/css-vars.js:45, 72-76`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/adapters/css-vars.js#L45), [`README.md:156`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/README.md#L156), [`src/types/index.d.ts:66-68, 172-176`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/types/index.d.ts#L66)
- **Problem:** `README.md` and TypeScript definitions document passing `{ interval: 60000 }` as the 3rd argument (`autoVars(rules, el, { interval: 60000 })`). However, `autoVars()` assumes `interval` is a primitive number. When an object is passed, `Date.now() % interval` evaluates to `NaN`, causing `setTimeout` and `setInterval` to continuously spin every ~1ms.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Accept both a number (`60000`) and an options object (`{ interval: 60000 }`).
  - [ ] Normalize interval: `const ms = typeof interval === 'object' && interval ? interval.interval ?? 60000 : Number(interval) || 60000`.
  - [ ] Add unit test verifying `{ interval: 60000 }` sets timer correctly without infinite spin.

---

### [ ] T02: Remove Broken `import { compile }` Conflict in `.d.ts` Declaration
- **Files:** [`src/types/index.d.ts:1, 148-150`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/types/index.d.ts#L1), [`package.json:28`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/package.json#L28)
- **Problem:** `src/types/index.d.ts` starts with `import { compile } from "../core/engine";` while line 148 declares `export declare function compile...`. This causes `TS2440` (import declaration conflicts with local declaration) and `TS2307` (`Cannot find module '../core/engine'`) when copied into `dist/`.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Remove the invalid relative import from `src/types/index.d.ts`.
  - [ ] Validate `.d.ts` compilation clean with `npx tsc --noEmit`.

---

### [ ] T03: Support `CompiledRules<T>` Across Core Functions in TypeScript
- **Files:** [`src/types/index.d.ts:103, 148-150, 160-163, 172-176, 198-202`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/types/index.d.ts#L103)
- **Problem:** `auto()`, `useAutoTheme()`, `observe()`, and `autoVars()` only type-accept raw rule arrays (`AutoRule<T>[]` or `AutoVarRule[]`), throwing TypeScript errors when developers pass pre-compiled rules from `compile()` per the documentation.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Update function signatures to accept `AutoRule<T>[] | CompiledRules<T>`.
  - [ ] Update `compile()` to accept `AutoRule<T>[] | CompiledRules<T> | AutoVarRule[]`.

---

### [ ] T04: Prevent Incomplete `since`/`until` Rules from Hijacking Daily Time Rules
- **Files:** [`src/core/engine.js:176-200`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/engine.js#L176-L200)
- **Problem:** In `compile()`, `else if (eachRule.time != null)` (line 176) and `else if (eachRule.day != null)` (line 191) precede `else if (eachRule.since != null || eachRule.until != null)` (line 195). A rule missing `until` like `{ since: '12-01', time: 18, style: 'winter' }` is silently pushed into `timeRules` and runs every single day of the year.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Move incomplete range check (`(eachRule.since != null) !== (eachRule.until != null)`) before evaluating `time` or `day`.
  - [ ] Emit `console.warn` and discard the invalid incomplete rule.

---

## 🟠 P1 — High (Logic Flaws, State Leaks & Edge Cases)

### [ ] T05: Support `day` Conditions in Composite Date and Date-Range Rules
- **Files:** [`src/core/engine.js:103-163, 187-189`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/engine.js#L103), [`src/core/utils.js:235-253`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/utils.js#L235)
- **Problem:** Composite rules combining a date or range with a day (e.g., `{ since: '06-01', until: '08-31', day: [0, 6], style: 'summer-weekend' }`) are placed in `dateRanges` or exact date buckets where `resolveRule()` never invokes `isDayMatch()`.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Check `isDayMatch(r, now)` when evaluating matched date ranges and exact dates.
  - [ ] Add test for date range + day combinations.

---

### [ ] T06: Fix `isEqual()` False-Positive Equality Bugs in React Hook
- **Files:** [`src/react/useAutoTheme.js:42-56`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/react/useAutoTheme.js#L42-L56)
- **Problem:**
  - Line 42 checks `if (Array.isArray(a))` without checking `if (Array.isArray(b))` when `a` is a plain object and `b` is an array.
  - Lines 53–55 iterate keys of `a` without checking `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(b, key)`. Objects with different keys having `undefined` values compare as equal.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Guard `Array.isArray(a) !== Array.isArray(b)`.
  - [ ] Verify `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(b, key)` for each key.
  - [ ] Add unit tests for asymmetric comparison edge cases.

---

### [ ] T07: Clean Up Stale Custom Properties in `autoVars()` When Rules Expire
- **Files:** [`src/adapters/css-vars.js:52-59`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/adapters/css-vars.js#L52-L59)
- **Problem:** `if (!matched || !matched.vars) return;` (line 54) exits before property removal (lines 57–59). When a temporary date or day rule expires and no new rule matches, injected CSS custom properties remain permanently stuck on the DOM element.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] When `!matched || !matched.vars`, clear all tracked variables from `compiled.allVarKeys` and return cleanly.
  - [ ] Add unit test verifying teardown on expired match.

---

### [ ] T08: Guard `observe()` Against Missing Config & Handle Mixed Style Transitions
- **Files:** [`src/core/observer.js:37-45, 66-90`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/observer.js#L37-L45)
- **Problem:**
  - Calling `observe()` or `observe(null)` throws unhandled `TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'target' of 'config' as it is undefined`.
  - Transitions between class strings and style objects fail to clear the opposing style mechanism.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Add default `config = {}` and validate `target` defensively.
  - [ ] If `previousStyle` was an object and `nextStyle` is a string, remove inline styles; if `previousStyle` was a string and `nextStyle` is an object, remove classes.

---

### [ ] T09: Preserve Pre-Existing Host Classes in DOM Adapter
- **Files:** [`src/adapters/dom.js:19-24`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/adapters/dom.js#L19-L24), [`src/core/observer.js:123-124`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/observer.js#L123-L124)
- **Problem:** `applyClasses` removes all tokens present in `previousClasses`. If the target element originally had a class in HTML before `observe()` was started (e.g., `text-black`), switching rules or calling `.stop()` strips the element's original class.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Snapshot the target element's initial classes when `observe()` starts.
  - [ ] Never remove classes that belonged to the initial class snapshot.

---

### [ ] T10: Harden Date, Time, and Day Bounds Checking Across Utils & Engine
- **Files:** [`src/core/engine.js:104-140, 150-193`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/engine.js#L104), [`src/core/utils.js:23-44, 158-179`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/utils.js#L23)
- **Problem:**
  - `isValidDate` string length check allows unhyphenated numeric dates like `20271031` through to `exactRecurring`.
  - `parseDate()` returns `NaN` values for non-numeric date components without error.
  - `parseTime()` accepts partial strings like `"10:20pm"`, `"12px"`, and `-0:30`.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Validate date formats strictly with regex: `/^(\d{4}-)?(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01])$/`.
  - [ ] Validate time strings strictly with regex: `/^([01]?\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\d)$/` and integers `0–23`.
  - [ ] Validate `day` against allowed strings and integers `0–6`.

---

### [ ] T11: Support Mixed-Format `since`/`until` Ranges (`YYYY-MM-DD` + `MM-DD`)
- **Files:** [`src/core/utils.js:131-142`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/utils.js#L131-L142)
- **Problem:** `isInDateRange()` requires both endpoints to have a year; if one has a year and the other does not, it silently ignores the year and evaluates as recurring annual.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] If one endpoint provides a year and the other does not, either infer current year or emit a clear warning during `compile()`.

---

### [ ] T12: Prevent Unhandled Crash in `useAutoTheme()` When `options` is `null`
- **Files:** [`src/react/useAutoTheme.js:59-64`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/react/useAutoTheme.js#L59-L64)
- **Problem:** `const { interval = 60000 } = options;` throws `TypeError` if a user calls `useAutoTheme(rules, fallback, null)`.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Safe default: `const { interval = 60000 } = options || {};`.

